  "steps": [
    {
      "text": "• Finely grate the ginger. Finely grate the garlic (or use a garlic press). In a medium saucepan, heat the butter and a dash of olive oil over a medium heat. Add the garlic and ginger and cook until fragrant, 1-2 minutes. Add the basmati rice, water (for the rice) and the salt, stir, and bring to the boil. Reduce the heat to low and cover with a lid. Cook for 10 minutes, then remove from the heat and keep covered until the rice is tender and the water has absorbed, 10 minutes.\n• TIP: The rice will finish cooking in its own steam so don't peek!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5e436f6ae0d90372b362e448/step-e315365b.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• While the rice is cooking, trim and halve the green beans. Thinly slice the capsicum. Thinly slice the cucumber. Slice the lemon (see ingredients list) into wedges. In a small bowl, combine the wasabi mayonnaise (if using) and water (for the mayo).\n• TIP: Wasabi has a strong horseradish flavour so use less if you aren't a fan or add a little plain mayo from the pantry to mellow the flavour.\n• TIP: Adding water to the wasabi mayo will make it easier to drizzle.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5e436f6ae0d90372b362e448/step-e6aa55d4.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• In a medium bowl, combine the plain mayonnaise and the pieces of Japanese tofu. Toss to coat. In a second medium bowl, combine the panko breadcrumbs and sesame seeds, then add the mayo-coated tofu to coat. Transfer to a plate.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5e436f6ae0d90372b362e448/step-9affb61a.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• When the rice has 10 minutes cook time remaining, heat enough oil to coat the base of a large frying pan over a medium-high heat. When the oil is hot, add the crumbed tofu and cook until golden, 2-3 minutes each side. Transfer to a plate lined with paper towel and season with salt and pepper.\n• TIP: Turn the tofu gently to prevent crumbs from falling off!",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5e436f6ae0d90372b362e448/step-f9a10f32.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Wipe out the frying pan with paper towel and return to a medium-high heat with a drizzle of olive oil. Add the green beans and cook until nearly tender, 3-4 minutes. Add the capsicum and cook until wilted, 1-2 minutes. Season with salt and pepper.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5e436f6ae0d90372b362e448/step-16c9633f.jpg"
    },
    {
      "text": "• Divide the garlic & ginger rice between bowls. Top with the crumbed tofu, sesame greens, cucumber and drizzle with the wasabi mayo (if using). Squeeze over the lemon wedges and drizzle with a little soy sauce to serve.",
      "imageUrl": "https://img.hellofresh.com/f_auto,fl_lossy,q_auto,w_800/hellofresh_s3/5e436f6ae0d90372b362e448/step-ef0adb59.jpg"
    }
  ]
